                <pb facs="0584" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg550"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 51.—Translation of
                        notice.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Exclusion of American meats by authorities of
                        Schaffhausen.</hi></head>
                <p>On examination of the provisions offered for sale in this city, it has transpired
                    that meats declared as picnic ham (picnic schinken), corned meat (pockelneisch),
                    etc., for the most part of American origin, have been preserved by a preliminary
                    treatment in which substances are used that are directly injurious to the
                    health.</p>
                <p>The employment of table salt and saltpeter alone is permitted for the
                    preservation of meat.</p>
                <p>The sale of meat otherwise prepared is therefore forbidden,.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Board of Health (Gesundheits Commission).</hi>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Schaffhausen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
